# Idris2 proof manifest — read by scripts/check-proofs.sh idris2
# Format: <source-root>|<module-relative-to-source-root>|gated|quarantine|<note>
# gated      = must compile.  quarantine = known-broken, must keep failing.
# Ground-truthed 2026-09-20 with idris2 0.7.0 (the version the estate pins, and the
# version these verdicts were measured against).
#
# There is no production code in this file that is quarantined: every Idris2 module
# in the repository compiles, and the four that used to sit in quarantine were
# repaired rather than tolerated.
#
# ─── The ABI seam: the modules that actually define the C ABI ─────────────────
# These live in src/interface/ beside the code they describe, not in this
# directory. They are gated here anyway, because a proof about the wire format
# that sits in another tree is a proof nobody updates when the format changes —
# and the whole point of the seam is that the header cannot move without the
# proofs moving with it.
src/interface|Abi/Types.idr|gated| the ABI model: struct fields, fixed-point, version, capability and action codes. Source of truth for the generated header.
src/interface|Abi/Layout.idr|gated| offset and size proofs for all seven structs, incl. ee_context (72 B). Offsets are proved over literal field lists; see the module header for why.
src/interface|Abi/Foreign.idr|gated| the tick model and the v0 decision rule (decide/tickModel) with their branch proofs. The kernel in src/core/kernel.zig implements this.
src/interface|Abi/Gen.idr|gated| the generator itself: cross-checks proven sizes against declared fields and emits ee.h + ee_layout.zig. Gated so a generator that stops compiling cannot pass CI while still producing a plausible header.
src/interface|Abi/Utility.idr|gated| Phase 2 slice 2: the utility graph — v0's branch chain written as scores and a maximum, so a behaviour can be added by adding a score. Gated because the claim of the slice is a THEOREM-shaped claim (the three pinned digests do not move) and this module is half of the evidence; the null hosts are the other half.
src/interface|Abi/Modes.idr|gated| Phase 2 slice 3: modes and commitment — the VSM S2 layer (ADR-0012). Five modes in three previously-undefined flag bits, and hysteresis by SCORE MARGIN (a Schmitt trigger) rather than by a dwell counter, so the only new state is the mode itself. Proofs: encoding round-trips, the mask is a multiple of two so a mode write cannot clobber the memory flag, commitment HOLDS a wounded engaged agent, and commitment RELEASES the moment a precondition fails or a real precedence (reload) applies. This is the first INV-category proof in the estate's own taxonomy: state-machine invariants.
src/interface|Abi/Memory.idr|gated| Phase 2 slice 1: perception memory (TTL, freshness, forgetting) and the memory-armed rule, with the TTL and the from-memory flag pinned by theorems. SPECIFICATION + WIRED: the Zig kernel implements this (commit 4db53ae), and `Memory.idr`'s prediction that the digest could not move was REFUTED by measurement — see ADR-0009 decision 5.
src/interface|Abi/Affect.idr|gated| ABI 1.1, mind slice 1 (ADR-0013): three leaky-integrator reservoirs, the affect token and its cause, the grievance-widened margin, the tells. GENERAL theorems: reservoirs stay in [0, full] (integrateInRange); the leak with no input never grows (leakNeverGrows) and strictly shrinks a non-empty reservoir (leakStrictlyShrinks), so it reaches zero; a token change has a cause and an unchanged token has none (tokenChangeHasCause, tokenKeptHasNoCause); grievance zero gives the 1.0 margin (calmMarginIsTheModesMargin); no damage capability keeps grievance at zero (noCapabilityNoGrievance); affect never writes a bearing (sightingIgnoresAffect, leadNeverInventsABearing). Instances pin the grudge override, its release, and that no affect holds against flight or reload.

